8d85-056330e87039","oracle_text":"You may tap or untap target artifact, creature, or land.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2003-07-28","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Emmara's ability is a triggered ability, not an activated ability. It doesn't allow you to tap Emmara whenever you want; rather, you need some other way of tapping it, such as by attacking.","oracle_id":"c65ba242-3369-48a9-864f-1b1f85238f67","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"For the ability to trigger, Emmara has to actually change from untapped to tapped. If an effect attempts to tap Emmara, but it was already tapped at the time, this ability won't trigger.","oracle_id":"c65ba242-3369-48a9-864f-1b1f85238f67","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Creatures are only put into a graveyard for having 0 toughness when state-based actions are checked. If Maro’s toughness goes to 0 during the announcement or resolution of a spell or ability and then goes back up above 0 before the end of that announcement or resolution, it won’t be put into your graveyard when state-based actions are checked.","oracle_id":"ef32258a-d567-4fbc-ab85-8c00080f5b36","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the target creature has an ability that triggers when it becomes tapped, that ability triggers before it loses all abilities.","oracle_id":"f712aed5-d6e0-45d3-ae20-518b765ce9da","published_at":"2018-04-27","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the target creature has power and toughness written as */* with an ability that defines its power and toughness, it’s 0/0 when it loses all abilities. If its power and toughness are written as */*+1, it’s 0/1, and so on.","oracle_id":"f712aed5-d6e0-45d3-ae20-518b765ce9da","published_at":"2018-04-27","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once you announce that you’re casting a spell or activating an ability, no player may take other actions until the spell or ability has been paid for. Notably, players can’t try to remove a permanent’s activated abilities to stop them from happening. Once activated, the ability on the stack will resolve even if the creature loses the ability.","oracle_id":"f712aed5-d6e0-45d3-ae20-518b765ce9da","published_at":"2018-04-27","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
